To upload your app update to Google Play Store:

## Steps to Upload New Version:

1. *Build your updated APK/AAB*
   - Update your version code and version name in pubspec.yaml
   - Run flutter build appbundle --release (for AAB) or flutter build apk --release

2. *Go to Google Play Console*
   - Sign in to your developer account
   - Select your app (SkyFeed)

3. *Create new release*
   - Go to "Production" (or "Testing" if you want to test first)
   - Click "Create new release"

4. *Upload your build*
   - Upload the new AAB/APK file
   - Google will analyze it and show any issues

5. *Update release details*
   - Add release notes describing your changes:

   - Streamlined news categories for better performance
   - Improved user interface and experience
   - Bug fixes and optimizations


6. *Review and rollout*
   - Review all details
   - Click "Start rollout to production"

## Important Notes:

- *Version increment*: Make sure you increased version: 1.0.1+2 in pubspec.yaml (both version name and build number)
- *Testing*: Consider using "Internal testing" or "Closed testing" first
- *Review time*: Updates typically take 1-3 days to be reviewed
- *Staged rollout*: You can release to a percentage of users first (e.g., 20%) then gradually increase

## Don't forget:
- Update the store listing description we just wrote
